{"id":"d-45905ca14b","area":"apps.chart.src.part1","claim":"File Open fails on a saved document containing a locked group with children because replacement adds the locked group first and the add path refuses children under it","where":"apps/chart/src/chartPersistence.ts:75","files":["apps/chart/src/chartPersistence.ts"],"severity":"medium","triage":{"scenario":"open a `.weaselchart.json` whose snapshot has a node with `locked: true` and a child under it (a locked container or group, e.g. saved by another weasel app or edited by hand). `replaceChart` lifts the lock guard only around `removeMany`; the `scene.add(spec)` loop runs guarded, so adding the child calls `refuse(parent, 'add under')` (packages/core/src/core/scene/treeEdits.ts:96) on the just-added locked parent and throws \"Scene: cannot add under …\". The batch fails and Open reports \"Could not open the file\" for a valid file. It should load the file as saved, with the lock last (as `docs/unruled.md`'s 2026-11-10 duplicate ruling does), e.g. by running the whole replacement inside `scene.unlocked`.","fix":["apps/chart/src/chartPersistence.ts"],"size":"line","cause":"lock guard lifted for removal only, not for restoring the saved nodes","confidence":"likely"},"status":"open","first":{"ledger":"apps.chart.src.part1@9c4522d635","commit":"9c4522d63555ec5f264441bcef4cd6a1917eac02"},"sightings":[{"ledger":"apps.chart.src.part1@9c4522d635","defect":"D1","occasions":[1,2],"sources":["codex","claude"]}]}
